.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_PROP_UPDATE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_prop_create_boolean ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_int ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_int_array ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_int64 ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_int64_array ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_string ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_string_array ,
.Nm ndi_prop_update_byte_array
.Nd create and update hardware properties
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_create_boolean
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_int
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "int data"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_int_array
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "int *data"
.Fa "uint_t nelements"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_int64
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "int64_t data"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_int64_array
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "int64_t *data"
.Fa "uint_t nelements"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_string
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "char *data"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_string_array
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "char **data"
.Fa "uint_t nelements"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_prop_update_byte_array
.Fa "dev_t match_dev"
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "uchar_t *data"
.Fa "uint_t nelements"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va match_dev
Device number associated with the property.
Use \fBDDI_DEV_T_NONE\fP for a property associated with the node as a whole.
\fBDDI_DEV_T_ANY\fP is not permitted.
.It Va dip
Device node whose hardware properties are changed.
.It Va name
Nonempty, null-terminated property name.
.It Va data
Value, array, or string to copy into the property.
.It Va nelements
Number of array elements, rather than the size in bytes, except
for the byte-array function.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions create or replace properties on the hardware property list of
\fBdip\fP.
A nexus uses this list to describe a child device that it has enumerated.
The property name and value are copied; the caller retains ownership of the
input storage and may reuse it after the call returns.
These functions do not modify firmware or the driver's software property list.
Use the DDI property lookup functions to read the resulting properties.
.Pp
\fBndi_prop_create_boolean()\fP creates a property whose presence represents true.
It has no data value.
Remove the property to represent false.
The integer functions store a single integer or an array of integers of the
specified width.
The string functions store a null-terminated string or an array of pointers to
null-terminated strings.
The byte-array function stores exactly \fBnelements\fP bytes.
Array lengths must be nonzero.
.Pp
An existing property with the matching device number and name is updated;
otherwise a property is created.
The caller must keep the device node valid throughout the operation.
When accessing properties through a driver's property entry point, the driver
must also be held.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user, kernel, or low-level interrupt
context.
Memory allocations do not wait for memory to become available.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return \fBDDI_PROP_SUCCESS\fP on success.
Failures include \fBDDI_PROP_INVAL_ARG\fP for invalid arguments,
\fBDDI_PROP_NO_MEMORY\fP for an allocation failure, and
\fBDDI_PROP_CANNOT_ENCODE\fP if a value cannot be encoded.
These are property status codes, not NDI status codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_prop_lookup 9F ,
.Xr ddi_prop_update 9F ,
.Xr ndi_prop_remove 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
